  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining CSS Configurations**\n\nI\'m working on adding utility classes and font configurations to `src/index.css`. I\'m exploring how to define utility classes using `@theme` in Tailwind CSS v4, considering both standard utility classes and base styles. Currently, I am focused on the structure of the `@layer base` block, specifically the `body` styling.\n\n\n**Refining Font Definitions**\n\nI\'ve added specific font families to `src/index.css`: a sans-serif for general use, and a serif option. I\'ve also implemented a `no-scrollbar` class for cleaner mobile scrolling, ensuring the horizontal scroller is hidden. These styles enhance visual presentation, especially the text readability.\n\n\n**Developing Event Configurations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining a data model and creating detailed decoration packages. I\'m starting with `src/types/decoration.ts` and `src/data/decorations.ts`, aiming to capture rich, realistic Kerala/Indian event aesthetics. This involves several wedding, engagement, and reception configurations with unique themes.\n\n\n**Cataloging Event Designs**\n\nI\'m cataloging various event designs, each with unique themes and aesthetics. I\'m focusing on \"Luxury Golden Glow Stage\" and \"Midnight Starlight Banquet Stage,\" including details like lighting, florals, and backdrops. Also, I am designing for haldi, mehndi, birthdays, anniversaries, baby showers, and traditional event entrances, creating a structured data model. I\'ll need IDs, names, and categories.\n\n\n**Structuring Event Metadata**\n\nI\'m structuring event metadata using categories like Haldi, Mehndi, and Birthdays, alongside styles such as Luxury and Traditional. I\'m focusing on attributes like short and full descriptions, features with icons, specs (setup time, etc.), and high-quality images. I\'m also including options for featured designs, most-loved status, color themes, and tags to enrich the catalog.\n\nI\'m now adding a moments gallery for real event photos from Perambra/Kerala using a masonry layout with a Lightbox viewer to enhance user engagement with the gallery. Moreover, I\'m integrating key features. The core of my current work is integrating a WhatsApp Enquiry System that pre-fills messages and provides a quick custom event enquiry modal, all without any pricing to drive customer interaction.\n\n\n**Designing Product Pages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the product detail page, implementing a multi-image gallery with a lightbox viewer, along with rich feature highlights and specifications. I\'m adding a \"Enquire on WhatsApp\" CTA. Additionally, I\'m designing a \"Share decoration\" button to enhance sharing. I\'m also including a recommendation carousel for related decorations, and breadcrumb navigation.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 150256132
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
